On Nov 28, 2:25 am, Jistan Idiot <jistanid...@gmail.com> wrote:
> So any advice other than quit now?

If you can't have immortality, you should set yourself up for the next
best thing: Escape the dungeon with enough gold and toys to make the
rest of your life *very* comfortable.

I would recommend:
- Good armour, weapons & spells, maxed levels, intrinsics and stats:
As a fearsome warrior you can raise an army, overthrow some local
town/ city/ nation and rule it as your own.
- Charm monster at 0% failure: For "persuading" your enemies to join
your cause, and to swell the ranks of your army.
- Saddled tame dragon or jabberwock: great for winning battles,
intimidating peasants, generally flying about on, and for guarding
your treasure room.
- As many tame foocubusses of appropriate gender as you can squeeze
through the upstairs, because, well... obviously...
- A few pet humanoids/ elves, levelled right up with good armour,
stats and weapons, to get your army started and to be your captains
when you'd rather be back at the castle with your concubines than out
in some muddy field conducting batles in person.
- Lots of gold and gemstones: For paying off those you can't
'persuade', and to boost the economy of your new kingdom and bring
prosperity to your people. Or for piling up in a big room and rolling
about in. Your choice.
- Blessed luckstone or two: So that things always seem to go your
way.
- Amulet(s) of lifesaving, unihorn, sources of healing. If your mortal
life is going to be so good, you want to make it last as long as
possible.
- Blessed figurines of useful monsters (including spare dragons,
foocubi, warriors)
- Source(s) of wishing: Again, just in case.





